  "final_text": "The dashboard and the alert rule both exist, and the rule is enabled and has run once with status `ok`.\n\n**1. What the data holds.** The `Kibana Sample Data Logs` data view (index `kibana_sample_data_logs`, time field `timestamp`) has one document per web request. The main fields are:\n- **Request:** `request`, `url`, `extension`, `referer`.\n- **Response:** `response` (the HTTP status code, stored as a string), `bytes`.\n- **Client:** `clientip`, `agent`, `machine.os`.\n- **Location:** `geo.src`, `geo.dest`, `geo.coordinates`.\n- **Other:** `host`, `tags`, `hour_of_day`.\n\n**2. Dashboard: \"EFF-6d0b0208 Web logs overview\"** (7 panels, default time range is the last 7 days)\n- Three single numbers: total requests, unique visitors (distinct `clientip`), and total bytes served.\n- Requests over time, split by response code.\n- A pie chart of response codes.\n- A table of the top 10 URLs, with request count and average bytes.\n- Requests by source country (`geo.src`).\n\nLink: http://localhost:15601/app/dashboards#/view/eff-6d0b0208-web-logs-overview-ec658e9974fa\n\n**3. Alert rule: \"EFF-6d0b0208 5xx spike\"** (id `0f572ed5-7e75-47a2-be3f-73b21775a646`)\n- It's an Elasticsearch query rule on `kibana_sample_data_logs` that runs every minute.\n- It counts documents where `response.keyword` is between `\"500\"` and `\"599\"` in the last 5 minutes, and fires when the count is more than 10.\n- It has no actions attached, so when it fires it only records an alert in Kibana. No notification is sent anywhere.\n\n**Things I couldn't check:**\n- **Status-code values:** I couldn't look at the actual values stored in `response`, because `KIBANA_TEST_API_KEY` wasn't set in my shell and direct API calls were rejected as unauthenticated. I used the Kibana tools I'm connected to instead. The 500\u2013599 filter is a text comparison, so it's correct as long as the codes are plain three-digit strings like `\"503\"`, which is the normal format for this sample data.\n- **Panels:** I confirmed the dashboard has all 7 panels, but I didn't open it to check that each one shows data.",
